<title>THAILAND: Thai Jan-Aug petroleum demand up 9.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Thai Jan-Aug petroleum demand up 9.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's petroleum demand in the first eight months of 1996 rose by 9.6 percent to 883,370 barrels per day (bpd) from the same period last year, the Petroleum Authority of Thailand (PTT) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Consumption of refined products rose 10 percent to average 729,510 bpd while the demand for natural gas went up 7.6 percent from the same period last year to the equivalent of 153,860 bpd, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Petroleum purchases in the first eight months of 1996 averaged 1,049,820 bpd, an 18.5-percent increase, from last year. Imports totalled 783,820 bpd--a 22.2-percent rise from the same period last year.</p>
<p>Procurement from local sources rose 8.8 percent to 266,000 bpd, the report said.</p>
<p>The PTT detailed January-August petroleum use and procurement as follows:</p>
<p>			 Average bpd	  Change from Jan-Aug 1995</p>
<p>Total consumption (by product)</p>
<p>Gas oil		 310,060	     up 13.9 pct</p>
<p>Fuel oil		172,880	     up  3.9 pct</p>
<p>Gasoline		118,800	     up  9.3 pct</p>
<p>Aviation fuel	  58,050	     up  2.4 pct</p>
<p>Liquid petroleum gas 52,430	     up 18.2 pct</p>
<p>Kerosene		  1,740	     dn  1.1 pct</p>
<p>Natural gas	   153,860	     up  7.6 pct</p>
<p>Others		   15,550	     up 20.6 pct</p>
<p>TOTAL		   883,370	     up  9.6 pct</p>
<p>Total procurement</p>
<p>Imported Crude oil  607,800	     up 36.2 pct</p>
<p>Gas oil		 100,050	     dn  8.1 pct</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 57,810	     dn  9.6 pct</p>
<p>Gasoline		  8,510	     dn 36.8 pct</p>
<p>Aviation fuel	   1,350	     dn 65.8 pct</p>
